<title>USA: FFO Financial Group Q4 net increases.</title>
<headline>FFO Financial Group Q4 net increases.</headline>
<dateline>ST. CLOUD, Fla. 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>THREE		  TWELVE</p>
<p>					MONTHS ENDED	 MONTHS ENDED</p>
<p>					  DECEMBER 31,   DECEMBER 31,</p>
<p>				   1996	1995	1996	1995</p>
<p> NET INTEREST INCOME	 2,676    2,316     9,974     9,619</p>
<p> PROVISION FOR LOAN LOSSES   625	152	 782	 477</p>
<p> NET EARNINGS		  1,479	490     1,600     1,646</p>
<p> EARNINGS PER SHARE	   0.18     0.06	0.19	0.20</p>
<p>(dollars in thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>NOTE:  Net income for fiscal 1996 included an FDIC special assessment of $1.5 million.</p>
<p>Net income for the fourth quarter of 1996 included a nonrecurring credit of $1.5 million reflecting a reversal of an excess provision for losses on real estate owned.</p>
<p>The weighted average number of shares outstanding during each of the periods was 8,430,000.</p>
<p>The fiscal 1996 provision for loan losses includes a $500,000 addition to the unallocated reserve made during the fourth quarter, due in part to the increase in the amount of loans outstanding.</p>
</text>
